# Build context filter for deploy/pi/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context's own
# `.dockerignore`, so this scopes the filter to the Pi image without adding a
# root-level file that every other build in the repository would inherit.
#
# This file is an optimisation — it keeps ~1 GB of host artefacts out of the
# context. It is *not* the safety mechanism: the Dockerfile deletes any
# `node_modules` that reaches it before installing, because a macOS arm64 tree
# copied into a linux/arm64 image is the exact failure this deployment cannot
# afford, and it would not surface until the first role call.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.vercel
coverage
**/coverage
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
supabase/.temp
supabase/.branches
.DS_Store

# No secret ever reaches a build layer. The exception comes last, because later
# rules win: the `.env.example` files are documentation and safe to carry.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
